{"grille" "The Grille was a series of self propelled artillery vehicles used by Nazi Germany during World War II. The Grille series was based on the Czech Panzer 38(t) tank chassis and used a 150mm sIG 33 infantry gun."}
; -- group cc5 --
; [new] card "nebelwerfer41" cost 450 lvl 1 | soldiers vehicle_supporter x2 | tags artillery rocket 44 45 43 42 41 | units/ger/vehicles_44.set:80 | also under ger_ss/v22; cards nebelwerfer41, nebelwerfer41_ss
{"nebelwerfer41" "The 150mm Nebelwerfer 41 was a German multiple rocket launcher used in the Second World War for saturating fire. Its main drawbacks included heavy smoke generated by the launchers which meant that it had to be relocated quickly due to counter-artillery."}
; -- group cc7 --
; [new] card "np_sdkfz251_1w" cost 1500 lvl 1 | soldiers vehicle_supporter x3 | tags artillery heavyart rocket 44 45 43 42 41 | units/ger/vehicles_44.set:86 | also under ger_ss/v22; cards np_sdkfz251_1w, np_sdkfz251_1w_ss
{"np_sdkfz251_1w" "The SdKfz 251 \"Stuka Zu Fuss\" was a German World War II multiple rocket launcher. Itwas equipped with the Wurfrahmen 40 (launch frame 40) launcher. (also known as a \"glorified wooden box\") It combined a vehicle such as the SdKfz 251 halftrack with rocket artillery to form a more mobile and protected artillery piece than the towed Nebelwerfer. It was nicknamed Stuka zu Fuss. (Stuka on foot)"}
; -- group cc1 --
; [new] card "flak18a" cost 600 lvl 1 | soldiers vehicle_supporter x2 | tags artillery 45 43 42 41 | units/vehicles_x.set:200 | also under ger_ss/v22; cards flak18a, flak18a_ss
{"flak18a" "The 88mm FlaK 18 was an anti-aircraft and anti-tank gun, mounted on a gun carriage that enabled it to fire in all directions. Widespread production started in 1933, and it soon proved to be the best anti-aircraft weapon available when Germany intervened during the Spanish Civil War. It also turned out to be an excellent anti-tank weapon, as its high muzzle velocity and large calibre gave it the power and range to take out enemy armour. The success of this weapon lead to many variants and it was one of the most recognizable German weapons throughout the war. This variant has APCBC and HE ammo available."}
; -- group cc4 --
; [new] card "morser18(ger)" cost 1150 lvl 1 | soldiers vehicle_supporter x2 | vehicles morser18 | tags artillery heavyart heavy 45 43 42 41 | units/ger/vehicles_45.set:68 | {info morser18}; also under ger_ss/v22; cards morser18(ger), morser18(ger_ss); copy of morser18 (with crew)
{"morser18" "The 210mm Morser 18 was a German heavy howitzer used in the Second World War by independent artillery battalions and batteries. It was one of the first weapons, if not the first in quantity production, that used the interesting dual-recoil system. If (and that's a big if) its shell hits its intended target, nothing survives in the path of its shockwave."}
